course: dictionary
lesson: 9202
title: Soggy: wet, soft and unpleasant
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: Soggy means very wet and soft, often in an unpleasant way. Think of soggy cereal, soggy grass after rain, or soggy shoes that squelch when you walk.
explain: Soggy can also describe food that has gone soft because it soaked up liquid or was kept too long. «In Dublin, Babcia sends a recipe for pierogi; theirs come out like soggy slippers.» Slippers are not for eating, so the word soggy tells you the dumplings were wet, soft and not nice.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. «Soggy leftover bread pollutes ponds» tells you the bread has gone wet and soft, and that it is bad for the water. Try a swap: put wet and soft into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: Soggy means very wet and soft.
fact: Soggy can describe food that has gone soft after soaking up liquid, like «soggy chips».
fact: Soggy usually sounds unpleasant: nobody wants soggy socks on a cold day.
fact: In science, soggy soil is full of water.
fact: Soggy is an adjective, so it can change form: soggier and soggiest compare how wet or soft things are.
exercise: Sam's socks were soggy after he splashed through the puddles. What does soggy mean? | *Wet and soft | Warm and dry | Very loud | Shiny and new
exercise: Which word could replace soggy in «soggy chips»? | crunchy | *wet and limp | hot | sweet
exercise: «Soggy leftover bread pollutes ponds.» Find and copy the word that tells you the bread has gone wet. | *soggy | pollutes | ponds | leftover
test: «The soggy field squelched under our boots after the storm.» What does soggy mean here? | Bright and sunny | Frozen hard | *Very wet and soft | Dry and dusty
test: The bread was even ___ after a night in the rain. Which word fits? | *soggier | soggiest | sogger | softer
exam: Jayden says soggy means shiny. What does soggy really mean? | Hard and crunchy | *Very wet and soft, often in an unpleasant way | Shiny and bright | Hot and steamy
